# API & Security

## Service layer

- All HTTP/API access in `services/` (or Route Handlers / Server Actions for Next.js-native paths).
- Services return typed results; throw or return `Result` types — no business logic in route files beyond orchestration.
- One shared client for auth headers, base URL, and error normalization when calling external APIs.

## Environment variables

- **Client-exposed:** `process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_*` only for non-secret config.
- **Server-only:** database URLs, API secrets, tokens — never import into Client Components.
- Do not use Vite-style `import.meta.env.VITE_*` in Next.js projects.

## Validation

- Validate all external input (forms, actions, route handlers) with Zod.
- Never trust client-side validation alone.

## Security

- No secrets in source control or client bundles.
- Sanitize user-generated content when rendered as HTML.
- Auth tokens: prefer HttpOnly cookies or secure patterns defined by the project; never log tokens.
- Map API errors to safe user messages; log details server-side only.

## Errors

- Distinguish validation, business, and infrastructure failures.
- Fail gracefully; avoid silent broken UI.
